Z||000000||Cozmo||12-30-2001||11:02 AM||||OK, I'm doing a Cadero and thanks to some great info from Cadero2dmax I've decided to use a cradle from an '88 on my "target" car ('87 Coupe).<BR>I've been following the Held group purchase thread but am unsure about the coilover strut requirements. I know I need the strut relocation brackets, but do I have to get the big $$$ Konis?<BR>Kinda seems to defeat the "spirit" of the Caddy swap, cost-wise...<BR>Ideas? Suggestions?<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Cardone</B><BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thankssig.jpg">   <BR><B>'85 2M6 SE Targa</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||cadero2dmax||12-30-2001||03:47 PM||||You need not spend th big $ on your conversion. I have an old set of Monroe struts on one car, and a set of Gabriel OEM replacement struts on the other. Or you could get KYB's, or even use what you have now.<P>You can get an adjustable perch kit from Held that will work, or from Ground Control, or from several other sources. I would suggest checking out Ground Control, they use an Eibach spring and I like their workmanship. Theirs, including all the necessary hardware, spring rate/size of your choice, etc are about $250 (if memory serves me). <P>The spring length depends on how much lower you want the rear end to sit. On the SE I have 8" springs on the rear coil-overs (300# springs, harsher ride, but I plan on autocrossing and doing some track days with the car) and Eibach lowering springs with an additional 1/4 coil cut out on the front.<P>Since you are planning the 4.x engine swap, might I suggest the CaderoOwnersForum@yahoogroups.com<BR>list? You will find others that have completed or are in the process of doing this swap.<P>Hope this helps<P><BR>------------------<BR>George Ryan<BR>A pair of 4.9 Cadero's<P>My former Q4 Fiero racecar<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Texas_Motor_Speedway_4.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
